<binaryimage arch="x86:LE:64:default:gcc">
<!--
    kuna #1918: a call's double result read with a 16-byte register move.

    findutils `pred_newer` (gcc -O2) calls the unprototyped `difftime` and
    moves its result with `movapd %xmm0,%xmm1` before zeroing `xmm0` with
    `pxor`. Both instructions are single 128-bit operations on the whole
    `XmmReg`, so the heritaged `xmm0` range is 16 bytes and the SysV return
    slot `XMM0_Qa` sits inside it. Without an output guard the call defines
    nothing in that range and the result prints as a variable no statement
    assigns.

    Synthetic reduction:
        1140  53                 PUSH     RBX
        1141  48 89 d3           MOV      RBX,RDX
        1144  e8 27 00 00 00     CALL     0x1170        ; result in XMM0_Qa
        1149  66 0f 28 c8        MOVAPD   XMM1,XMM0     ; 16-byte read of xmm0
        114d  66 0f ef c0        PXOR     XMM0,XMM0
        1151  f2 48 0f 2a c3     CVTSI2SD XMM0,RBX
        1156  f2 0f 58 c1        ADDSD    XMM0,XMM1
        115a  5b                 POP      RBX
        115b  c3                 RET
    and the callee, with no symbol and so no prototype:
        1170  48 29 f7           SUB      RDI,RSI
        1173  66 0f ef c0        PXOR     XMM0,XMM0
        1177  f2 48 0f 2a c7     CVTSI2SD XMM0,RDI
        117c  c3                 RET

    Stage: P3 heritage call guarding, option calloverlap. Pass 1 (off) pins
    the bug; pass 2 (the default auto) gives the call the float return slot at
    the low end of the wider register and the sum reads it.
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x1140">
534889d3e827000000660f28c8660fefc0f2480f2ac3f20f58c15bc3
</bytechunk>
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x1170">
4829f7660fefc0f2480f2ac7c3
</bytechunk>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x1140" name="f"/>
</binaryimage>
<script>
  <com>option calloverlap off</com>
  <com>lo fu f</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>option calloverlap auto</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>quit</com>
</script>
<stringmatch name="CALLOVERLAP FLOATRET #1: off, the call defines no result" min="1" max="1">^  sub_1170\(a0,a1\);</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="CALLOVERLAP FLOATRET #2: off, the sum reads a variable nothing assigns" min="1" max="1">return \(float8\)a2 \+ v1;</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="CALLOVERLAP FLOATRET #3: auto, the sum reads the call's result" min="1" max="1">return \(float8\)a2 \+ \(float8\)sub_1170\(a0,a1\);</stringmatch>
</decompilertest>
